    'Relationship psychology taxonomy',
    'Connects cognitive distortions and mismatched response styles to intimacy conflict.',
    'When a relationship conflict feels bigger than the event, check the filter. Mindreading turns silence into proof. Overgeneralizing makes one failure into destiny. Personalization makes another person''s mood an accusation. Polarized thinking turns repair into winning or losing. Response-mode mismatch adds friction: one partner wants logic, one wants feeling, one needs sensation, one needs action, one reaches for distance. The seed should help a character misread believably and then repair specifically.',
