    'Tracks hidden contracts, unrealistic expectations, money pressure, and stress overflow into intimacy.',
    'Relationship expectations often arrive unspoken: courtship energy will last, personality will not change, money values match, sex needs align, domestic labor will feel fair, stress will not change tenderness. When the contract is invisible, conflict sounds petty. Track which expectation was verbalized, hidden, inherited, self-imposed, outdated, or unrealistic. Then track what pressure touches it: work, money, children, time, fatigue, illness, status, privacy, or shame. Repair starts when the expectation becomes speakable.',
    array[
