    'This source leans on older men-talk-this-way and women-talk-that-way frameworks. Keep them as cultural scripts, not laws. Useful routes: a character has absorbed the script, a couple discovers it does not fit them, a narrator critiques it, a therapist reframes it, or a dated source shapes someone''s expectations. Modern prose should name behavior directly: interrupts, fixes, withdraws, asks, reassures, avoids, performs competence, overexplains, seeks validation, or cannot bear conflict. Do not flatten people into gender categories.',
    array[
