    'When a scene stalls, identify desire, danger, and decision. What does the character want to get, keep, escape, prevent, or risk accepting? What human value is at stake: love, dignity, safety, freedom, belonging, justice, status, truth, control, or self-respect? Then force a decision that changes the situation. Every meaningful action should create a new fact the next turn has to live with.',
    array[
      'desire-danger-decision-triad',
      'desire-get-keep-escape-prevent',
      'major-dramatic-question',
      'causal-event-chain',
