    'Roleplay pacing taxonomy',
    'Adapts the eight-sequence model into a flexible roleplay arc from inciting pressure through aftermath.',
    'For long-form roleplay, track which pressure phase the scene resembles without announcing it in prose. Setup and challenge create the hook. Reluctance and commitment make agency visible. Early action tests the wrong assumptions. First failure reveals cost. Midpoint changes the map. Recommitment raises personal stakes. Second attempt creates crisis. Climax turns theme into action. Resolution shows what the characters now have to live with.',
