    'Escalation taxonomy',
    'Separates revelation, recommitment, catastrophe, and final action so a story can keep building.',
    'Do not spend the whole middle repeating the same pressure. A midpoint should change what the character understands. A recommitment should change why or how they act. A crisis should cost them what they thought they had secured. A climax should require the one choice they could not have made at the start. This creates escalation that feels earned rather than louder.',
