    'Use tropes as raw material, not prefab story. For each trope, tag its degree, type, and role. Degree: primary engine or secondary accent. Type: person, place, object, relationship, institution, or structural device. Role: secret, change, pressure, misdirection, promise, or reveal. Then connect it to GMC: what does the character want, why does it matter, what blocks it, and what risk becomes visible because this trope exists? A trope earns its place when it creates conflict, reveals character, or tightens genre promise.',
