    'Before stacking tropes, give each major character a working GMC. Goal should be concrete enough to succeed or fail. Motivation should carry emotional charge: love, freedom, justice, survival, shame, revenge, belonging, ambition, or protection. Conflict should make the goal harder in a way that fits the trope. If the goal changes, update the trope pressure. A familiar trope becomes sharp when it collides with a specific why.',
