    'genre-contract-trope-map',
    'Genre trope taxonomy',
    'Keeps trope use aligned with the promise of romance, mystery, thriller, fantasy, science fiction, or mash-up stories.',
    'Route every trope through the leading genre promise. Romance needs the relationship question honored, usually through HEA or HFN. Mystery needs the central puzzle answered. Thriller needs escalating danger and a live push-pull with opposition. Suspense needs dread, uncertainty, and consequence. Fantasy needs world logic that pressures character. Science fiction needs premise, technology, species, time, or scale to alter the problem. In mash-ups, name the lead contract first so secondary tropes enrich the story instead of pulling it apart.',
