    'In mystery, suspense, and thriller work, treat the cast as a pressure system. Antagonists need GMC, not just menace. Victims matter more when they disturb the protagonist or community. Suspects need secrets that may or may not touch the central crime. Red herrings misdirect through plausible motive, incomplete evidence, or withheld context. Bosses, rookie partners, antiheroes, neighbors, workplace allies, and recurring community figures should each add pressure, information, obstruction, or emotional cost.',
