    'scene-goal-conflict-disaster-router',
    'Scene craft taxonomy',
    'Routes scene beats through goal, conflict, disaster, sequel, and next-goal causality.',
    'Use this source when a scene needs stronger cause and effect. Name the scene goal first: what does the character want right now, and how does it serve the larger plot? Then name the conflict: who or what blocks it, and why does that opposition matter personally? End with a disaster or qualified outcome that answers the scene question and creates the next pressure. After the disaster, give the character enough reaction, dilemma, and decision to make the next move feel earned.',
    array[
      'scene-structure-goal-conflict-source',
      'scene-goal-domino-chain',
      'integral-conflict-opposition',
      'scene-disaster-outcome',
      'reaction-dilemma-decision-sequel',
