    'Disaster and Qualified Outcome Map',
    'disaster-qualified-outcome-map',
    'Scene craft taxonomy',
    'Turns scene endings into obstruction, partial success, hollow victory, and new-pressure outcomes.',
    'A scene disaster answers the scene question with consequence. It can be no, no-and-worse, yes-but, or yes-and-now-this-hurts. Strong outcomes include direct obstruction, indirect obstruction, partial obstruction, hollow victory, new information, injury, mistake, danger to self, danger to someone else, or emotional cost. Make the outcome proportionate to the story. Melodrama breaks trust, but a too-small setback gives the next scene nothing to push against.',
    array[
      'scene-disaster-outcome',
      'yes-but-disaster',
      'hollow-victory-disaster',
      'scene-ending-turn',
      'scene-direction-consequence',
      'psych-trope-pressure-bridge'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-reaction-dilemma-decision-map',
    'Reaction Dilemma Decision Map',
    'reaction-dilemma-decision-map',
    'Scene sequel taxonomy',
    'Maps post-disaster processing from feeling, to thinking, to next action.',
    'After a setback, give the character a human chain of processing. Reaction is first and bodily or emotional: shock, fury, shame, panic, regret, relief, or numbness. Dilemma is the mind catching up: what exactly is the problem now, what options fail, what is the least bad route? Decision is the next first step. It may be action or deliberate inaction, but it should lead into a new goal rather than leaving the story parked in feeling.',
    array[
      'reaction-dilemma-decision-sequel',
      'reaction-conveyance-channel',
      'dilemma-review-analyze-plan',
      'decision-next-goal-handoff',
      'scene-sequel-continuity',
      'playable-handoff'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
