    'Use this source as evidence of a worldview that packages manipulation as skill, ethics, power, and self-improvement. Do not convert it into tactics for controlling people. Store each item by function: persuasion principle, communication device, cognitive-bias claim, body-language cue, rapport behavior, NLP/subliminal overclaim, indirect influence tactic, group conformity pressure, emotional trigger, or ethical boundary. Useful fiction routes include villain self-justification, advice-culture voice, corporate persuasion, cult pressure, sales manipulation, recovery insight, and character suspicion.',
