    'Rapport and boundary taxonomy',
    'Separates genuine connection from performed similarity, emotional anchoring, and covert leverage.',
    'Mirroring can be social ease, empathy, survival, flirtation, salescraft, or manipulation. Anchoring can be memory, ritual, grounding, trauma cue, brand association, or covert emotional leverage. Sort by transparency, intent, reciprocity, boundary respect, and target effect. Ethical use makes another person safer and freer to choose. Risky use makes them feel obligated, softened, dependent, confused, or easier to steer.',
