    'Use psychological triggers as pressure labels, not control buttons. Self-image, loss fear, belonging hunger, injustice anger, unfinished tasks, emotional contagion, bystander diffusion, groupthink, labels, humblebragging, reverse psychology, and subliminal/NLP claims can all shape behavior in fiction. Keep the effect probabilistic and contextual. Stronger scenes show the pressure meeting a specific wound, group, reward, fear, or need, then show the consequence when the person notices they were being steered.',
