    'Do not write male orgasm as a single mechanical event. Separate arousal build, subjective pleasure, ejaculation, orgasm, satisfaction, aftereffect, and emotional meaning. A character may ejaculate without feeling satisfied, feel pleasure without ejaculation, lose rhythm from stress, or need reassurance after a body response does not match the scene goal. In prose, the difference appears through breath, muscle tension, focus, relief, frustration, embarrassment, pride, tenderness, cleanup, and what the character says afterward.',
