    'Turns polarized beliefs about monogamy, nonmonogamy, desire, jealousy, and blame into usable character psychology.',
    'When a character argues about fidelity, track the belief before the behavior. Common polarities: monogamy is natural versus oppressive; nonmonogamy is honest versus selfish; jealousy is proof of love versus cultural programming; cheating means no love versus unmet need; biology explains behavior versus excuse-making. Mentalization asks the character to hold more than one mind at once: what I wanted, what you felt, what the rival believed, what the agreement was, what harm happened, and what repair would cost.',
