    'Love Triangle Role and Accountability Map',
    'love-triangle-role-accountability-map',
    'Relationship psychology taxonomy',
    'Maps each person in a love triangle by motive, injury, fantasy, responsibility, and available next move.',
    'A love triangle is not one wound told three times. Give each role its own pressure. The unfaithful partner may want relief, novelty, admiration, secrecy, revenge, proof of desirability, or two incompatible lives. The betrayed partner may face trauma, rage, humiliation, intuition, denial, evidence hunger, and the decision to stay or leave. The affair partner may face hope, waiting, self-blame, moral conflict, rivalry, and the promise that keeps moving. Accountability asks what each person knew, chose, hid, endured, repaired, or refused to repair.',
    array[
      'love-triangle-role-map',
      'affair-partner-ambivalence-bind',
      'affair-accountability-catalyst',
      'emotional-affair-boundary',
      'psych-attachment-rupture',
