    'Attachment and Narcissism Infidelity Risk Map',
    'attachment-narcissism-infidelity-risk-map',
    'Character psychology taxonomy',
    'Keeps attachment insecurity and narcissistic defenses as risk variables rather than verdicts.',
    'Use attachment and narcissism as pressure, not destiny. Anxious characters may pursue, monitor, plead, retaliate, or panic over rival threat. Avoidant characters may compartmentalize, distance, hide, or seek low-demand intimacy elsewhere. Grandiose narcissistic defenses may chase conquest, admiration, exception status, or entitlement. Vulnerable defenses may seek reassurance, revenge, or proof they are still wanted. None of these labels replaces scene evidence: what did the character do, what did they know, and how did they respond when harm became visible?',
    array[
      'attachment-infidelity-risk',
      'narcissistic-infidelity-defense',
      'dark-triad-infidelity-caveat',
      'psych-attachment-activation',
      'attachment-insecurity-abuse-caveat',
      'psych-trust-calibration'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
