    'Connects betrayal, rival comparison, self-worth injury, possessiveness, and revenge motives.',
    'After betrayal, the injury may land as desire lost, status lost, body shame, public humiliation, sexual comparison, or fear of being replaceable. Jealousy can become information, protest, control, revenge, or self-protection. Retaliatory infidelity needs a motive label: punishment, pride repair, equalizing pain, proving desirability, numbing humiliation, escaping helplessness, or trying to make the partner finally understand. In modern prose, show it through small evidence: checking, rehearsed indifference, a changed outfit, a cruelly timed confession, or the silence after a rival name.',
    array[
