    'Before and during any physically complex scene, track where each character is, which way they face, what supports each person''s weight, which limbs are free, and which areas are reachable, blocked, exposed, or hidden. Change one variable at a time: angle, pressure, rhythm, balance, proximity, or orientation. Let bodies react to friction, fatigue, leverage, breath, strain, sensory overload, interruption, climax, conflict, or emotional realization.',
