    'Connects desire, arousal, anatomy, physical response, and emotional context without treating one body model as universal.',
    'Ground physical response in character, context, and individual variation. Desire may be shaped by safety, novelty, taboo, confidence, stress, threat, trust, fantasy, touch, relationship tension, or emotional state. Body response should be observable through breath, approach, hesitation, tension, sensitivity, fatigue, avoidance, changed risk threshold, or contradiction. Avoid universal response rules; treat anatomy and physiology as adaptable constraints rather than a fixed script.',
