    'Anatomy and physiology',
    'Uses touch, pressure, rhythm, breath, sound, temperature, texture, and reaction as concrete scene evidence.',
    'Sensory writing should name what causes the sensation and how the body responds. Track touch, pressure, texture, temperature, rhythm, breath, sound, scent, balance, muscle tension, and changing sensitivity. Keep sensory detail tied to contact, environment, movement, emotion, and character meaning. Do not stack vague intensity words; make the reader understand what changed physically and why it matters.',
    array[
