    'Positioning and Spatial Geometry',
    'positioning-spatial-geometry',
    'Physical reference',
    'Tracks facing, distance, support, sightlines, furniture, exits, blocked movement, and reachable contact.',
    'Establish scene geometry before escalating physical action. Track where each body is, which way each person faces, what furniture or surface is involved, what supports weight, what is reachable, what is blocked, what is exposed, what remains hidden, and what exit or privacy constraints exist. A new action may require a transition: shifting knees, turning hips, bracing hands, changing angle, moving clothing, adjusting height, or changing balance.',
