    'Romance craft taxonomy',
    'Keeps romance relationship, both lead arcs, and external plot pressure moving together.',
    'A romance can go slack when the relationship, lead arcs, and plot stop talking to each other. Map each scene across four tracks: what changes between the leads, what changes in lead A, what changes in lead B, and how the external situation forces contact or choice. The plot spine should put the leads close enough to irritate, see, desire, misunderstand, and finally choose each other with eyes open.',
