    'core-falling-in-love-vulnerability-ladder',
    'Falling-in-Love Vulnerability Ladder',
    'falling-in-love-vulnerability-ladder',
    'Romance pacing taxonomy',
    'Stages romantic change from ordinary-world defense to new perception, commitment, exposure, and critical decision.',
    'Stage the romance as pressure on old protection. First, show the defense in ordinary life. Next, let falling in love make a different life imaginable: new light, new curiosity, new irritation, new tenderness. Then commitment raises vulnerability and the old defense stops working. Passion, sex, intimacy, or emotional closeness can reveal the fear directly. End the stage with a critical decision that costs the old self something real.',
    array[
      'ordinary-world-self-protection',
      'falling-in-love-belief-challenge',
      'commitment-vulnerability-exposure',
      'passion-sex-fear-reveal',
      'romance-leap-of-faith',
      'psych-intimacy-vulnerability'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-love-interest-essence-mirror-map',
    'Love Interest Essence Mirror Map',
    'love-interest-essence-mirror-map',
    'Relationship arc taxonomy',
    'Uses the love interest as mirror, challenge, and invitation toward the lead''s truer self.',
    'The love interest should not function as therapist or prize. They embody or provoke the essence the lead is afraid to live. They recognize a truer nature under the mask, but recognition alone is not rescue. Scene work: the love interest names a strength, refuses a performance, sees through a defense, creates safety, creates conflict, or becomes the person whose loss would prove the old belief has won. The lead still has to choose the change.',
    array[
      'lover-recognizes-true-nature',
      'love-interest-embodies-essence',
      'relationship-barrier-internal-conflict',
      'antagonist-foil-arc-reflection-map',
      'mutual-longing',
      'psych-conflict-repair'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
