    'Use status-genre structure when the story pressure turns on respect, rank, reputation, public failure, class mobility, creative recognition, professional ascent, romantic social proof, or belonging inside a hierarchy. Name the visible success yardstick, then name the private wound it tempts. Track audience, antagonist, foil, mentor, shapeshifter, moral challenge, inner obstacle, and likely bittersweet cost. A status story is strongest when the climb changes what success means.',
