    'respect-self-esteem-status-arc-map',
    'Character arc taxonomy',
    'Separates the protagonist''s hunger for respect from the deeper need for self-worth.',
    'In a status arc, the want is usually legible from across the room: promotion, title, invitation, applause, money, publication, victory, marriage, access, or public respect. The need is quieter: self-esteem, dignity, belonging without performance, integrity, or the courage to stop begging the wrong crowd for proof. Keep both active. Every victory should ask whether the character is becoming more whole or just better dressed in the old wound.',
    array[
