    'Scene function taxonomy',
    'Makes status pressure visible through audience, rules, rank markers, and consequences.',
    'Status scenes need a visible measuring system. Define who is watching, what counts as winning, what counts as shame, who gets to judge, and what the judgment changes. Public witness can be a ballroom, office, family dinner, school hall, group chat, award stage, courtroom, fandom, campus, court, bedroom rumor network, or tiny room where one person represents the whole world. Let the audience alter behavior: posture, diction, risk, restraint, bravado, silence, or a choice made only because someone saw.',
    array[
