    'Character role taxonomy',
    'Uses antagonist, foil, mentor, and shapeshifter roles to pressure the protagonist''s definition of success.',
    'Assign status-story roles by function, not label. The antagonist threatens position or exposes the cost of the climb. The foil shows another path to success, whether healthier, uglier, cheaper, or freer. The mentor offers a map, but the map may be outdated, self-serving, or partial. The shapeshifter destabilizes trust by changing allegiance, image, story, or apparent values. Each role should force the protagonist to ask whether they want respect, power, admiration, safety, revenge, or self-respect.',
    array[
      'antagonist-position-threat',
      'foil-alternative-success-path',
      'status-mentor-guidance',
      'status-shapeshifter-hindrance',
      'antagonist-foil-arc-reflection-map',
