values
  (
    'core-six-stage-hero-arc-source-router',
    'Six Stage Hero Arc Source Router',
    'six-stage-hero-arc-source-router',
    'Routes a short hero-arc handout into persona, essence, wound, stage ladder, relapse, climax, and resolution taxonomy.',
    'Use this source for protagonist transformation, especially when the story needs a clean map from self-protection to honest action. Store: persona, essence, wound, premise pressure, stage one mask, stage two glimpse, stage three gradual shift, stage four backslide, stage five arrival, and stage six changed self. Keep examples out; keep the reusable craft structure.',
    'Do not make the wound decorative or resolve it in one speech. Do not force every genre to show the same amount of visible growth.',
    array[
      'six-stage-hero-arc-source',
      'persona-to-essence-arc',
      'wound-tied-to-premise',
      'growth-change-distinction',
      'psych-character-flaw'
    ],
    array['hero arc', 'persona', 'essence']
  ),
  (
    'core-persona-wound-premise-map',
    'Persona Wound Premise Map',
    'persona-wound-premise-map',
    'Connects the protagonist''s coping mask to a wound that the premise will keep pressuring.',
    'Design the wound so the premise knows where to press. Ask what hurt taught the character to hide, what mask grew around it, what the mask costs, and why this specific story makes that defense fail. The wound should not sit in a dossier. It should alter choices: avoiding intimacy, performing toughness, controlling the room, staying useful, refusing help, or making jokes before anyone sees too much.',
    'Do not use trauma as flavor text. Do not expose private pain before the active POV has earned or discovered it.',
    array[
      'persona-coping-mask',
      'wound-tied-to-premise',
      'protagonist-flaw-pressure',
      'weakest-spot-attack',
      'pov-perception-boundary'
    ],
    array['coping mask', 'premise pressure', 'wound']
  ),
  (
    'core-six-stage-transformation-ladder',
    'Six Stage Transformation Ladder',
    'six-stage-transformation-ladder',
    'Maps transformation from full persona through glimpse, gradual shift, relapse, arrival, and honest resolution.',
    'Track the arc as staged erosion, not instant enlightenment. Stage 1: the mask works badly but feels safe. Stage 2: the character glimpses a freer self. Stage 3: action changes before belief catches up. Stage 4: the old defense fails and the character backslides. Stage 5: the climax demands essence-level action. Stage 6: resolution shows the new self in behavior, not a lesson recited aloud.',
    'Do not turn the ladder into rigid formula. Adjust intensity by genre, scope, and how much change the story can honestly bear.',
    array[
      'stage-one-full-persona-setup',
      'stage-two-glimpse-essence',
      'stage-three-change-in-motion',
      'stage-four-backslide-dark-moment',
      'stage-five-essence-arrival-climax'
    ],
    array['six stages', 'backslide', 'climax arrival']
  ),
  (
    'core-backslide-dark-moment-arc-map',
    'Backslide Dark Moment Arc Map',
    'backslide-dark-moment-arc-map',
    'Uses relapse into persona as the pressure point before irreversible change.',
    'The backslide is useful because it proves the old strategy no longer works. Let the character run to the familiar defense: anger, isolation, control, charm, denial, duty, pride, or withdrawal. Then make the cost clear. The audience should feel why the mask was tempting and why it cannot carry the character through the next choice.',
    'Do not make relapse a reset button. Do not punish vulnerability just to manufacture a dark moment.',
    array[
      'stage-four-backslide-dark-moment',
      'events-erode-persona',
      'protagonist-flaw-pressure',
      'moral-dilemma-catalyst-change',
      'psych-character-flaw'
    ],
    array['backslide', 'dark moment', 'old defense']
  ),
  (
    'core-essence-resolution-behavior-map',
    'Essence Resolution Behavior Map',
    'essence-resolution-behavior-map',
    'Proves final transformation through changed action, transparency, and a healthier relationship to self.',
    'At the end, show the new self doing something the old persona could not do. They tell the truth, ask for help, stay present, leave a false safety, choose love without ownership, accept loss without performing indifference, or act with courage after fear is named. Resolution can be quiet; it only needs visible behavior that proves the mask no longer has the final word.',
    'Do not let a tidy speech replace changed conduct. Do not imply healing is complete just because the plot is over.',
    array[
      'stage-five-essence-arrival-climax',
      'stage-six-resolution-honest-self',
      'persona-to-essence-arc',
      'growth-change-distinction',
      'theme-character-arc-map'
    ],
    array['changed action', 'honest self', 'resolution']
  )
