    'core-intro-revision-feedback-map',
    'Intro Revision Feedback Map',
    'intro-revision-feedback-map',
    'Uses reader response to tune the intended opening impression.',
    'After drafting an introduction, compare the intended impression with what readers actually report. Revise motivation, emotional reaction, scene emphasis, and visible behavior until the page points cleanly at the story you mean to start.',
    'Do not defend a confusing opening by explaining it outside the text. Avoid overcorrecting into exposition when the fix is sharper behavior, cleaner stakes, or a more legible reaction.',
