    'Separates real sexual reputation and safety risks from manipulative use of shame or trauma claims.',
    'The source sometimes notices real pressures and then bends them into tactic. Preserve the real categories: sexual double standards, fear of judgment, pregnancy risk, physical safety, prior harm, social stigma, and needing trust before privacy. Quarantine the manipulative leap: using those risks to create plausible deniability, exploit fear, or push past words. In fiction, this can explain guardedness, not authorize pressure.',
    array[
