    'Groups future pacing, disqualifiers, negging, leave-on-read scarcity, and emotional rollercoaster claims.',
    'Scarcity and future-pacing tactics create character pressure by managing distance, attention, and imagined payoff. Track whether the move is playful, mutual, and easy to refuse, or whether it creates insecurity, humiliation, confusion, or chase. Disqualifiers and teasing can be banter; negging uses a small wound to pull proof. Future pacing can be romance; manipulation uses fantasy to hurry attachment without substance.',
    array[
