    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-visible-character-specificity-map',
    'Visible Character Specificity Map',
    'visible-character-specificity-map',
    'Character description taxonomy',
    'Turns habits, gestures, lumpy details, and context shifts into readable character differentiation.',
    'Make characters distinct through behavior the scene can see. Useful fields: hand use, facial habits, posture, walking rhythm, clothing oddity, nervous tic, object handling, food sounds, glasses adjustment, distraction, eagerness to please, and how these change around family, work, friends, strangers, or a lover. A visible habit should do story work: reveal stress, self-protection, class, vanity, fatigue, repression, desire, or a lie.',
    array[
      'lumpy-parts-mannerism',
      'gesture-body-language-differentiation',
      'social-context-behavior-shift',
      'character-description-by-action',
      'emotion-description-bank',
      'phys-spatial-awareness'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-pov-reputation-perspective-drill-map',
    'POV Reputation Perspective Drill Map',
    'pov-reputation-perspective-drill-map',
    'POV and reputation taxonomy',
    'Uses POV shifts, other people''s descriptions, gossip, and reputation gaps to reveal character from multiple angles.',
    'A character is not the same object from every angle. Rewrite a pivotal scene from another viewpoint; describe a body through three observers; let strangers gossip; let a loved one notice different evidence than an enemy. Track what changes: sensory focus, moral judgment, missing information, class bias, attraction, resentment, grief, and what the narrator cannot admit. The gap between reputation and selfhood is often where pressure lives.',
    array[
      'pov-shift-character-reveal',
      'other-people-eyes-reputation',
      'character-reputation-gossip-gap',
      'pov-perception-boundary',
      'psych-social-mask',
      'reputation-access-stakes'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-character-pressure-exercise-map',
    'Character Pressure Exercise Map',
    'character-pressure-exercise-map',
    'Character pressure taxonomy',
    'Reveals character through moral dilemmas, mundane errands, crisis objects, public performance, and younger-self reflection.',
    'Pressure exercises work when they make choice visible. Put the character in an ordinary errand and let habit carry the scene. Put them in crisis and watch what object they grab first. Give them a public interview and see what they polish. Write the letter they would send their younger self. Force the one moral dilemma that contradicts their self-image. Each exercise should reveal priority, shame, tenderness, fear, or an action they cannot take back.',
    array[
