  (
    'core-outline-logline-scene-purpose-map',
    'Outline Logline Scene Purpose Map',
    'outline-logline-scene-purpose-map',
    'Outlining taxonomy',
    'Uses lists, loglines, three-Cs clarity, main/subplot tables, and scene-purpose audits to get drafts out of the swamp.',
    'When a draft turns muddy, compress it. Write the logline with character, conflict, and clarity. List possible endings, twists, subplots, growth turns, and setting details. Put main plot and subplots in parallel so each subplot complicates the protagonist journey. Audit every major scene for purpose: what changes, what question sharpens, what information arrives, and what becomes harder.',
    array[
