    'Use this source as a map of what characters may believe, justify, fear, or misread after infidelity. Keep the useful structures: secrecy damage, accidental boundary drift, romantic crisis flight, parallel-life arrangements, conquest scripts, revenge affairs, and repair pressure. Modernize the lens. Do not treat old gender claims, moral certainty, insulting labels, or blame language as truth. Store those pieces as character worldview, social myth, family pressure, or biased narrator material.',
