    'Uses affair timing to reveal life-stage panic, grief, aging fear, humiliation, success shock, or unwanted adulthood.',
    'When an affair begins near a life transition, ask what the character cannot bear to feel plainly. Possible triggers: parent death, childbirth, children leaving home, career collapse, career success, illness, aging, addiction pressure, public failure, boredom after stability, or a marriage that no longer lets them perform the self they miss. The affair can be intense and still be evasive. Let the romance expose the pressure; do not let it erase the breach.',
