    'If affair intensity starts behaving like self-medication, track the dose: secrecy, risk, sexual novelty, being needed, being chosen, rescue drama, forbidden tenderness, or proof that the character is still alive to someone. Then track the withdrawal: guilt, panic, boredom, disgust, grief returning, the old marriage problem still waiting, or a demand that the affair partner become a full life instead of an escape route.',
