    'Writing Vivid Emotions Router',
    'writing-vivid-emotions-router',
    'Descriptive vocabulary',
    'Routes emotion writing into POV feeling, observed cues, reader emotion, and revision safeguards.',
    'Use this source as an emotion-technique map, not a phrasebook. First decide whose emotion is being conveyed: the viewpoint character''s felt emotion, another character''s observed emotion, or the reader''s induced emotion. Then choose the right channel: visceral sensation, visible body cue, dialogue, voice, thought, description, simile, silence, contradiction, or pacing. Keep the prose vivid and lean: one precise cue beats a paragraph of explanation.',
    array[
      'writing-vivid-emotions-source',
      'pov-emotion-triad',
      'visceral-reaction-pov',
      'observed-body-language-cues',
      'reader-emotion-engine',
