    'Reader emotion comes from immersion, recognition, and controlled information. Put the reader inside the viewpoint character''s sensory and emotional filter, but allow the page to carry hints the character misreads or avoids. Use common human situations, concrete memory hooks, tonal word choice, and selective detail to stir dread, hope, shame, tenderness, suspicion, or relief. Never make boredom contagious. If the character is bored, write the pressure under the boredom.',
    array[
      'reader-emotion-engine',
      'pov-emotion-triad',
      'mood-filtered-description',
      'pov-grounded-simile',
      'stakes-reminder-strategy',
      'playable-handoff'
