    'Kink taxonomy',
    'Separates tactile sensual play from pain-centered intensity so scenes can carry kink through softness and attention.',
    'Sensation play does not need to escalate into pain to matter. Track caress, kissing, grooming, massage, tickling, licking, temperature, wax, ice, feathers, fur, oil, food texture, pressure, restraint-adjacent stillness, and the emotional charge of focused attention. In literary modern prose, write the cause and response: what touches, what changes in breath or posture, what feels exposed, what becomes funny, tender, sharp, or too much.',
