    'NSFW vocabulary',
    'Classifies body-part slang without letting crude or insulting language replace clear physical description.',
    'For anatomy slang, separate the body part from the register. Store canonical anatomy, common adult alias, crude alias, comic alias, porn alias, insult/slur flag, clarity risk, and character-voice fit. Prefer plain direct language when the scene needs clarity. Use crude terms only when they match a character''s voice, a negotiated dynamic, or a deliberate tonal choice. Do not let slang blur body mechanics, consent, pain, health risk, or the user character''s agency.',
    array[
