    'Use questionnaire fields only when they change story behavior. Strong fields: self-definition, strongest motive, future hope, feared future, biggest regret, strength, weakness, social style, role in story, effect on plot, key relationships, private contradiction, and what they would never admit aloud. Avoid trivia unless it creates action: dinner preference matters only if it reveals class, ritual, care, disgust, memory, or conflict.',
