    'A character becomes vivid when another character changes around them. Track what each person wants, fears, performs, hides, envies, gives, and withholds. Then write the contact effect: after talking to this person, does the other character feel braver, smaller, exposed, amused, defensive, desired, used, seen, or cornered? Relationship dynamics should leave fingerprints on voice, posture, risk, and next choice.',
