    'public-power-archetype-map',
    'Status and influence',
    'Maps bosses, enforcers, demagogues, envoys, justiciars, and administrators through public authority, persuasion, fear, and institutional leverage.',
    'Public-power archetypes should show how authority is made visible. A boss owns turf; an enforcer knows who can be held overnight; a demagogue turns grievance into applause; an envoy survives by making enemies listen; an administrator knows which paper opens the door. Track what kind of power they use, who grants it, who fears it, and what private weakness makes them overuse it.',
