    'care-deathwork-duty-map',
    'Character archetypes',
    'Pairs healer and deathwork backgrounds through duty, disgust tolerance, ritual, grief, power, and failure.',
    'Care and deathwork characters know what other people avoid looking at. Healers may confuse patients with puzzles, mistake competence for kindness, or carry every failure home. Morticians, graverobbers, and undertakers may use gallows humor, superstition, perfume, quiet movement, ritual, or greed to survive the work. Let the history show in small habits: clean hands, precise notes, too much calm, a joke that lands wrong, or a tenderness reserved for the dead.',
