  (
    'core-trauma-background-boundary-map',
    'Trauma Background Boundary Map',
    'trauma-background-boundary-map',
    'Trauma context',
    'Routes enslavement, war-survivor, and horror-witness backgrounds through agency, aftermath, stigma, and recovery rather than aesthetic trauma.',
    'Use trauma-heavy backgrounds as context, not decoration. Track what happened, what the character believes it means, what they avoid, what reflex survived, who they protect, what institution failed them, and what kind of dignity they are trying to recover. Former enslavement, war displacement, and impossible-horror witness material should create agency, solidarity, grief, anger, avoidance, nightmares, refusal, or repair. Do not eroticize captivity or suffering; do not make trauma the whole person.',
