    'Sexual education taxonomy',
    'Routes the LoveSex model into mind/body/brain/emotion education, sexual self-esteem, shame, anatomy literacy, safer sex, and trauma-aware boundaries.',
    'Use this source as psychosexual education taxonomy, not as substitute therapy or medical advice. Its useful frame is integration: mind holds beliefs, language, culture, and choice; body holds anatomy, breath, sensation, and physiology; brain holds arousal, memory, reflex, and desire circuits; emotion holds shame, truth, pleasure, pain, trauma, and relationship meaning. For fiction and roleplay, this model helps a scene ask what layer is speaking when a character wants, freezes, performs, refuses, or reaches for closeness.',
