    'Sexploration Exercise Governance Map',
    'sexploration-exercise-governance-map',
    'Safety and exercise taxonomy',
    'Keeps sexual self-exploration exercises choice-led, trauma-aware, and appropriate to context.',
    'If adapting sexual exploration exercises, begin with governance. The participant chooses, pauses, skips, adapts, and stops. Activation signs matter: numbness, panic, dissociation, intrusive memory, shame spiral, pain, or pressure to comply. The goal is quality of attention, not speed, volume, performance, or completion. In fiction, exercise refusal can be the therapeutic work: a character finding a no, being believed, and discovering that desire does not have to arrive on command.',
    array[
      'sexploration-exercise-governance',
      'trauma-aware-sexual-exploration',
      'psych-consent-boundaries',
      'nsfw-consent-boundary-risk',
      'content_boundary'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-sexual-self-esteem-map',
    'Sexual Self-Esteem Map',
    'sexual-self-esteem-map',
    'Character psychology taxonomy',
    'Builds sexual self-esteem from dignity, knowledge, curiosity, boundaries, and embodied choice.',
    'Sexual self-esteem is not being constantly desirable or technically impressive. It is the felt right to have a body, preferences, limits, curiosity, awkwardness, and pleasure without self-erasure. Track what strengthens it: accurate knowledge, kind inner speech, consent honored, pleasure named, shame softened, body respected, and relationships that can hear a no. Track what damages it: ridicule, coercion, disgust, silence, comparison, trauma, body shame, and performance pressure.',
    array[
