  ),
  (
    'core-body-naming-anatomy-literacy-map',
    'Body Naming and Anatomy Literacy Map',
    'body-naming-anatomy-literacy-map',
    'Anatomy vocabulary taxonomy',
    'Links accurate anatomy, personal language, shame, register, and body-specific pleasure literacy.',
    'Body language carries history. Track accurate anatomy names, private slang, family euphemisms, shame words, vulgar words, clinical words, romantic words, and which terms a character can or cannot say. Useful corrections include vulva versus vagina, clitoris as more than a visible bud, penis and scrotum distinctions, pelvic nerves, arousal changes, and the fact that anatomy varies. In prose, the right word should fit the character, the heat level, and the trust in the room.',
    array[
