      'sexual-language-register',
      'anatomy-homology-analogy',
      'sexual-health-literacy',
      'sexual-shame-guilt-distinction'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-sexual-shame-regulator-map',
    'Sexual Shame Regulator Map',
    'sexual-shame-regulator-map',
    'Emotion and shame taxonomy',
    'Treats sexual shame as a relational signal with protective, silencing, and repair functions.',
    'Shame can close the body before a character understands why. Track trigger, body sign, inner voice, audience, concealment, anger, collapse, performance, and repair bid. Shame may be protective when something feels socially unsafe; it may be destructive when it becomes permanent self-disgust. Fictional repair is rarely one speech. It is a sequence: being received, not mocked, allowed to stop, allowed to want, and given language that does not make the body disappear.',
    array[
      'sexual-shame-regulator',
      'sexual-shame-guilt-distinction',
      'sexual-shame-origin',
