    'Keeps sexual violence material in trauma, recovery, culture, prevention, and support context rather than eroticization.',
    'Sexual violence belongs in harm, prevention, recovery, social context, justice, and trauma routing. Do not turn it into erotic prompt fuel. For character work, track impact: body memory, shame, anger, numbness, relationship fear, medical context, disclosure, disbelief, support, and rebuilding choice. For source governance, preserve the category because it explains real behavior and social injury; keep the writing careful, non-sensational, and centered on agency and aftermath.',
    array[
      'sexual-violence-education-context',
      'trauma-aware-sexual-exploration',
      'content_boundary',
      'blocked',
      'psych-consent-boundaries'
