    'Social confidence taxonomy',
    'Turns approach-anxiety advice into low-stakes social practice without entitlement to a result.',
    'Approach practice should train presence, not conquest. Stages: get out, observe the room, talk to people generally, make a small remark, listen, share something real, tolerate awkwardness, leave cleanly, and stop measuring success only by a number or date. Rejection exposure is useful only when it preserves other people''s comfort and autonomy. In fiction, approach anxiety can show up as rehearsed lines dying in the throat, a too-bright laugh, a graceful exit, or the quiet pride of trying without making the other person responsible for the outcome.',
    array[
