    'Communication taxonomy',
    'Separates playful banter from actual connection, listening, specificity, and reciprocal curiosity.',
    'Banter can open a door, but connection gives the room somewhere to go. Track whether teasing lands, whether the other person gets to define themself, whether the speaker listens, whether substance appears, and whether play becomes pressure. Good conversation has a pulse: observation, response, small disclosure, shared humor, changed topic, pause, and a clean exit or next invitation. If the talk is all jokes, tests, and labels, the scene can go brittle. Add one true thing and watch the chemistry change.',
    array[
