    'Treat the "friend zone" as mismatched expectations, not a trap one person owes the other an escape from. A character with romantic interest can name it directly. The other person can say no, offer friendship, hesitate, or clarify an existing relationship. The interested character then chooses: genuine friendship without covert pressure, respectful distance, or a clean end. Watch for manipulative friendship, emotional-crutch resentment, jealousy, and entitlement. A strong scene lets refusal stand and makes self-respect quieter than punishment.',
