  ),
  (
    'core-arousal-threshold-pacing-map',
    'Arousal Threshold Pacing Map',
    'arousal-threshold-pacing-map',
    'Adult body-response taxonomy',
    'Maps arousal as a moving threshold rather than a binary switch.',
    'Track arousal as a live curve. Useful beats: low attention, warming interest, steady rise, plateau, near-threshold intensity, pause, breath, drop, return, overshoot, sudden loss, renewed focus, and post-orgasm sensitivity. Do not turn pacing into mechanical arithmetic. A number can help an author stage escalation, but prose should stay in sensation, choice, breath, muscle tension, humor, embarrassment, and the small decisions that change a scene. Threshold pacing is especially useful for edging, interruption, nervousness, delayed gratification, stamina anxiety, and scenes where control is part of the emotional risk.',
