    'solo-partner-practice-disclosure-map',
    'Consent and communication taxonomy',
    'Separates private experimentation from partnered scenes that need disclosure, consent, and shared expectations.',
    'Private practice can stay private; partnered practice changes the scene. Track whether the partner knows the goal, wants to participate, understands the pace, can stop, and is not being used as a prop for someone else''s self-improvement project. In roleplay, this creates good tension: awkward confession, playful curiosity, wounded pride, patient coaching, boredom, laughter, jealousy of the goal, or a partner asking to be wanted instead of managed. Use disclosure to humanize the scene, not to turn it into a checklist.',
    array[
