    'After orgasm, do not flatten the body into one expected response. Track sensitivity, warmth, lost focus, continued arousal, erection change, wetness, soreness, breathlessness, laughter, shakiness, pride, disappointment, embarrassment, tenderness, irritation, cleanup, and the decision to continue or stop. A partial success can be narratively richer than perfect control. Let aftermath reveal character: who reassures, who jokes, who withdraws, who wants data, who wants touch, who needs space, and who turns a failed experiment into intimacy.',
