    'Use body-awareness training as a literary tool: breath getting too fast, jaw clenching, thighs shaking, attention narrowing, a laugh breaking tension, soreness arriving late, a pause becoming more honest than performance. The point is not mastery porn; the point is presence. Let the character notice and adjust. Let awkwardness stay human. Let effort reveal vulnerability. This frame works for sensual pacing, stamina anxiety, athletic training parallels, trauma-sensitive pacing, disability-aware intimacy, and any scene where the body has its own vote.',
