    'Soft Conflict Safety Premise Map',
    'soft-conflict-safety-premise-map',
    'Boundary and tone taxonomy',
    'Preserves consequence while routing gruesome or permanently damaging outcomes away from the playable premise.',
    'Use soft conflict when the story needs rivalry without brutality. The rule is not no stakes; the rule is no gruesome collapse. Convert harm into status loss, embarrassment, depleted confidence, lost favor, delayed plans, changed alliances, damaged trust, or comic inconvenience. The safety premise can override realism when the genre frame depends on buoyancy. This is useful for cozy rivalry, court comedy, fairy-tale politics, school-of-magic social pressure, and any scene where defeat should sting without breaking the toy.',
    array[
      'soft-conflict-non-gruesome-premise',
      'content_boundary',
      'psych-pacing-escalation',
      'playable-handoff',
      'theme-chaos-order'
