-- ============================================================================
-- Section: Dark-psychology bundle source, manipulation taxonomy, mind-control claim caveat, NLP/persuasion overclaim, body-language lie detection, narcissist-empath scripts, digital influence, and empathy-boundary taxonomy
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Derived from structural analysis of:
-- /Users/meganmckinnon/Downloads/Archive/470349455-Manipulation-6-books-in-pdf.pdf
--
-- Source inspection notes:
-- - PDF title metadata: Manipulation - 6 books in 1: Dark Psychology, How to Analyze People,
--   Influence People, Emotional Intelligence, Narcissist, Empath.
-- - Author metadata: Ryan Dark. Created by calibre in 2020.
-- - 549 pages, roughly 184k extracted words.
-- - This pass mines the table of contents and opening representative sections only.
-- - The source mixes self-protection, persuasion, pop psychology, NLP/mind-control claims,
--   body-language certainty claims, narcissist/empath scripts, emotional intelligence,
--   and digital conversation advice.
-- - These seeds preserve taxonomy, character-belief evidence, and detection vocabulary.
--   They do not provide manipulation instructions, coercive persuasion guidance, hypnosis
--   instructions, or claims that body language/NLP reliably reveals or controls people.

