    'Keeps body-language and lie-detection vocabulary useful while blocking overconfident certainty claims.',
    'Use body-language material as possible scene evidence, not a truth machine. Gestures, posture, breathing, voice, gaze, stillness, and facial expression can suggest stress, concealment, attraction, fear, performance, habit, culture, disability, fatigue, or context. They do not prove lying on their own. For prose, body language is strongest when paired with stakes: what the character hides, what the observer wants to believe, what alternative explanation exists, and what behavior changes after the read.',
