    'Routes narcissist/empath pop-psych scripts into character belief, abuse recovery, boundary repair, and overlabeling caution.',
    'Narcissist/empath scripts are culturally powerful and often overused. Store them as belief-source and recovery vocabulary unless a real clinical context is established. Useful buckets: love bombing, silent treatment, fear, social-media control, sexual leverage, admiration hunger, declining self-esteem, codependency, empathy overabsorption, boundary collapse, no-contact framing, grounding, grief, anger, support, and confidence repair. Avoid using pop labels as a shortcut for complexity. Write behavior, impact, and recovery need first; labels come second, if at all.',
