    'Classify everyday couple problems by the active strain: poor communication, mismatched desire, money conflict, broken promise, substance-use disruption, low respect, past-relationship residue, jealousy, control, family pressure, social stigma, isolation, low self-esteem, or abuse. Separate ordinary conflict from danger. Ordinary conflict can route toward repair, clearer agreements, accountability, and changed habits. Abuse, coercion, stalking, threats, violence, or trapped isolation route to safety and boundary handling, not relationship-coaching beats.',
