    'Communication failure is often a time-and-courage problem before it is a vocabulary problem. Track who avoids, who pursues, what topic never gets a full room, what gets squeezed between tasks, what silence protects, and what misunderstanding repeats because no one slows down. Repair requires protected attention, plain language, questions that are not traps, and behavior that proves the conversation mattered. In prose, show the missed opening: the phone face-down, the sentence swallowed, the kettle boiling over while both pretend it is nothing.',
