    'Money conflict is rarely just arithmetic. Track spender/saver style, income gap, debt, family background, class shame, secret purchases, dependency, who pays, who decides, who feels controlled, and what spending symbolizes: freedom, safety, love, status, revenge, panic, or care. Healthy conflict needs transparency and boundaries. Coercive money control, trapped dependency, threats, or surveillance route to control and safety handling.',
