    'Trust repair taxonomy',
    'Tracks how repeated unreliability, lying, cheating, and apology failure weaken trust over time.',
    'A broken promise creates two problems: the thing not done and the new uncertainty about whether the person can be trusted. Track promise type, frequency, stakes, excuse pattern, apology quality, repair action, and whether the harmed partner has stopped believing future pledges. In fiction, erosion is powerful because it is cumulative: one missed call may not matter, but the third one lands on every earlier disappointment. Repair needs changed behavior under pressure, not better wording.',
