values
  (
    'core-infidelity-typology-source-router',
    'Infidelity Typology Source Router',
    'infidelity-typology-source-router',
    'Relationship damage taxonomy',
    'Routes affair-source material by motive, secrecy pattern, agreement breach, self-justification, and aftermath.',
    'Classify infidelity by function before writing consequence. Buckets: accidental boundary failure, crisis-romance escape, marital arrangement, conquest habit, revenge or power restoration, rescue fantasy, depression escape, loneliness, entitlement, conflict avoidance, or identity repair. Then track the breach: sexual exclusivity, emotional exclusivity, disclosure rule, health rule, money, time, public humiliation, child involvement, or reality distortion. Do not use affair typology to excuse harm. Use it to make self-justification, injury, repair, and consequence more precise.',
    array[
      'infidelity-typology-source',
      'relationship-agreement-boundary',
      'betrayal-reconciliation',
      'psych-self-justification',
      'post-betrayal-defensiveness',
      'belief-source-reference'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-accidental-infidelity-risk-zone-map',
    'Accidental Infidelity Risk Zone Map',
    'accidental-infidelity-risk-zone-map',
    'Relationship boundary taxonomy',
    'Maps accidental-affair setup conditions without treating carelessness as fate or consent.',
    'Use accidental-infidelity routing when the story involves a careless boundary collapse rather than a long planned affair. Risk zones include travel, alcohol, professional trips, lonely transitions, flattery, peer modeling, feeling undesired, politeness pressure, secrecy opportunities, poor marital attachment, and refusing to leave a charged situation. The useful beat is the small decision that could still have gone another way. Afterward, route by choice: confession, concealment, blame-shift, repetition, fantasy escalation, or concrete prevention.',
    array[
      'accidental-infidelity-risk-zone',
      'lying-primary-betrayal-injury',
      'relationship-agreement-boundary',
      'emotional-consent-alignment',
      'erotic-conversation-boundary',
      'psych-accountability-pressure'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-romantic-affair-crisis-flight-map',
    'Romantic Affair Crisis-Flight Map',
    'romantic-affair-crisis-flight-map',
    'Relationship psychology taxonomy',
    'Classifies intense affair romance as possible escape from grief, depression, aging, pressure, failure, or unwanted adulthood.',
    'When an affair feels like salvation, ask what reality it lets the character avoid. Triggers can include grief, parent death, children leaving home, first child arriving, health crisis, addiction pressure, job success, job failure, aging, humiliation, or a marriage that is too sane to hold the fantasy. The affair partner may function as drug, mirror, rescue project, rebellion, proof of desirability, or door out of numbness. Keep the heat and the delusion distinct: intensity can be real and still be a bad compass.',
    array[
      'romantic-affair-crisis-flight',
      'affair-as-depression-escape',
      'affair-partner-rescue-fantasy',
      'psych-attachment-activation',
      'psych-character-flaw',
      'betrayal-trigger-reminder'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-marital-arrangement-encapsulation-map',
    'Marital Arrangement Encapsulation Map',
    'marital-arrangement-encapsulation-map',
    'Relationship structure taxonomy',
    'Tracks parallel relationships used to keep a marriage stable but emotionally distant.',
    'A marital arrangement uses an outside bond to keep the inside bond from fully dying or fully healing. Track what the arrangement provides: sex, warmth, money, caretaking, romance, conflict avoidance, fantasy, status, or a place to put the unsolved part of the marriage. Then track what it freezes: honest repair, separation, grief, anger, sexual negotiation, practical independence, or a clean ending. This is not the same as ethical nonmonogamy; secrecy, unequal knowledge, and denied choice change the structure.',
    array[
      'marital-arrangement-encapsulation',
      'alternative-relationship-structure',
      'relationship-agreement-boundary',
      'implicit-monogamy-contract',
      'lying-primary-betrayal-injury',
      'new-monogamy-agreement'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-philandering-gender-power-belief-router',
    'Philandering Gender-Power Belief Router',
    'philandering-gender-power-belief-router',
    'Belief-source and character motive taxonomy',
    'Keeps conquest, gender resentment, masculinity/femininity proof, and entitlement scripts as flawed character-worldview material.',
    'Use philandering scripts as belief-source evidence, not diagnosis or truth. Possible motives: proving masculinity, proving desirability, punishing a gender, avoiding equality, collecting admiration, refusing vulnerability, measuring worth through conquest, or converting fear into charm. Route harmful claims carefully: misogyny, homophobia, entitlement, violence, manipulation, and dehumanizing labels belong in boundary or character-bias handling. A character may believe the script; the system should understand the wound, the harm, and the social myth that carries it.',
    array[
      'philandering-gender-power-script',
      'gendered-infidelity-belief-source',
      'revenge-affair-power-restoration',
      'promiscuity-stigma-agency',
      'gender-essentialism-boundary',
      'psych-coercive-control'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-lying-primary-betrayal-injury-map',
    'Lying as Primary Betrayal Injury Map',
    'lying-primary-betrayal-injury-map',
    'Betrayal repair taxonomy',
    'Separates the sexual breach from the injury caused by secrecy, denial, and distorted reality.',
    'After an affair, the sex may be only one part of the wound. Track the lie system: omitted facts, denied suspicion, minimized contact, false timeline, edited emotion, hidden money, health risk concealment, gaslighting-adjacent reassurance, and making the betrayed partner live inside a false story. Repair requires more than ending contact. It needs truth, consistency, answered questions, changed access, health accountability, patience with triggers, and no demand that the hurt partner become calm on schedule.',
    array[
      'lying-primary-betrayal-injury',
      'post-betrayal-defensiveness',
      'betrayal-trigger-reminder',
      'betrayal-reconciliation',
      'psych-accountability-pressure',
      'psych-conflict-repair'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-child-secret-triangulation-boundary-router',
    'Child Secret Triangulation Boundary Router',
    'child-secret-triangulation-boundary-router',
    'Family harm and boundary taxonomy',
    'Routes child involvement in adult affairs through divided loyalty, secrecy burden, parentification, and repair.',
    'If children are pulled into affair secrecy, classify it as family-boundary harm. Risk forms: using a child as messenger, asking them to lie, making them keep one parent''s secret, confiding sexual or romantic details, recruiting them against the other parent, using them as proof of who is right, or making them manage adult grief. Fiction may show the harm and its aftermath, but should not normalize the burden. Repair means removing the child from the triangle, restoring age-appropriate truth, and accepting that trust may not return on command.',
    array[
      'child-secret-triangulation',
      'lying-primary-betrayal-injury',
      'post-affair-triangulation-coercion',
      'relationship-agreement-boundary',
      'content_boundary',
