-- ============================================================================
-- Section: Social status psychology, dominance-prestige pathways, status-power distinction, impression management, hierarchy emotion, nonverbal rank cues, and inequality taxonomy
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Derived from structural analysis of:
-- /Users/meganmckinnon/Downloads/Archive/460775061-2014-Book-ThePsychologyOfSocialStatus-pdf.pdf
--
-- Source inspection notes:
-- - Edited academic volume: The Psychology of Social Status, Joey T. Cheng,
--   Jessica L. Tracy, and Cameron Anderson (eds.), Springer, 2014.
-- - 363 pages, roughly 176k extracted words.
-- - This pass mines the stable top-level vocabulary from the preface, contents,
--   opening chapter, and targeted searches rather than exhaustively seeding every chapter.
-- - Useful taxonomy: dominance and prestige as rank pathways; status versus power;
--   allocation bias; personality, stature, prosociality, impression management, emotion,
--   inequality, hormones/neural systems, and nonverbal status cues.

