    'Separates reusable romance-affection categories from gendered, age-ambiguous, or consent-risk checklist claims.',
    'Use viral romance checklists as belief-source material, not as universal truth. Extract the category behind the item: affection, reassurance, public validation, gift token, protective gesture, comfort, playful touch, romantic setting, or contact cadence. Then route the risk: age ambiguity, gender mind-reading, surprise touch, restraint, tickling, pressure to perform affection publicly, or ignoring a stated wish for space. For contemporary adult fiction, write the wish as character-specific: this person likes this kind of care, from this partner, in this context.',
