    'Affection bids work when they answer a character need rather than perform a generic list. Buckets: touch, held gaze, slow kiss, offered clothing, cuddling, sitting close, hand-holding, back rub, private joke, shared photo, walk, dance, rain moment, or quiet physical nearness. Track who initiates, who receives, whether the gesture is welcome, what it says that dialogue cannot, and what changes afterward. Keep the prose lean and specific: a borrowed sweatshirt can mean comfort, claim, scent, memory, or a reason not to leave yet.',
