    'Use snowflake expansion when a story needs shape before detail. Start with a one-sentence premise that names pressure and theme. Expand to a short paragraph with major turns. Add character summaries with goal, motive, inner conflict, outer conflict, false belief, and epiphany. Expand each plot sentence into a fuller movement, then build a scene list. Keep every expansion provisional: it should reveal missing pressure, not trap the story in a brittle outline.',
