    'Plot taxonomy',
    'Turns mystery, opportunity, threat, hardship, and relationship into modular stakes for novel and roleplay prompts.',
    'Build story momentum by stacking one or more hooks. Mystery creates a live question. Opportunity gives the protagonist a door worth opening. Threat makes delay costly. Hardship gives emotional weight and backstory pressure. Relationship gives the story something personal to risk. A scene does not need all five, but a weak premise often lacks at least one: no question, no chance, no danger, no wound, or no one the character can lose.',
    array[
      'mothr-story-hook-stack',
      'theme-scene-pressure',
      'hero-want-need-objective',
      'inner-life-surface-problem',
