    'Plot taxonomy',
    'Maps a story through set-up, wrong path, compressed options, revelation, all-is-lost, twist, and payoff.',
    'Use four-part pacing as a pressure audit. Part one plants the ending, introduces the false belief, and creates the first major shift. Part two lets proactive characters chase the wrong path until discovery points them elsewhere. Part three tightens external and internal obstacles until options shrink and the key truth becomes visible. Part four drives action, false success, all-is-lost, final reversal, and earned success or consequence. Each part should change what the protagonist thinks will save them.',
