    'Keeps deep backstory available to the writer while selecting only the details that pressure the current scene.',
    'A dossier is private fuel, not a chapter dump. Store birth context, family, school, work, money, politics, faith, friendship, relationship status, worldview, personality, triggers, joys, fears, skills, and secrets. Then choose what the scene needs: a behavior, hesitation, false assumption, competence, scar, debt, habit, or tender point. Good backstory is felt before it is explained. It should change choices, not sit politely in a profile field.',
