    'Sex-Difference Research Caveat Protocol',
    'sex-difference-research-caveat-protocol',
    'Source governance',
    'Keeps sex-difference findings useful without turning averages, dated samples, or theory claims into character law.',
    'Before using sex-difference material, tag the caveat layer: population, country, era, age, relationship status, sexual orientation scope, sampling method, self-report limits, wording, overlap between groups, and whether the claim is average difference, theory, author interpretation, or social script. Modern roleplay should treat gender as context, not destiny. Use the source to create pressure, expectation, shame, mismatch, or belief conflict; then let the individual character override the average when their history says so.',
    array[
      'sex-difference-research-caveat',
      'sexual-research-literacy',
