    'core-evolutionary-sex-difference-belief-router',
    'Evolutionary Sex-Difference Belief Router',
    'evolutionary-sex-difference-belief-router',
    'Source governance',
    'Routes evolutionary sexuality claims as theory lens, belief source, or character worldview rather than absolute truth.',
    'When a source explains sexuality through evolution, classify the claim before using it. Buckets: parental investment, mate choice, short-term sex interest, jealousy type, visual arousal, status/resource preference, youth/appearance preference, partner-number interest, or reproductive-risk logic. Then add counterweights: cultural learning, individual variation, queer and trans contexts, socioeconomic context, relationship agreement, and source-era limits. A character may believe the model fiercely; the system should keep theory, stereotype, and lived personhood separate.',
    array[
      'evolutionary-sex-difference-model',
      'sex-difference-research-caveat',
      'gender-essentialism-boundary',
      'belief-source-reference',
      'sexual-culture-source-governance'
