    'Gendered Sexual Script Map',
    'gendered-sexual-script-map',
    'Relationship psychology taxonomy',
    'Maps learned initiation, restraint, gatekeeping, desirability, and performance roles as modifiable scripts.',
    'Treat sexual scripts as learned pressure. Common moves: one person must initiate, one must slow down, one must prove desire, one must prove restraint, one must look desirable without seeming too eager, and one must read refusal as challenge or rejection. These scripts can be repeated, resisted, misread, or unlearned. For contemporary prose, write the pressure in behavior: a hand that stops short, a joke that tests permission, a partner who waits to be wanted, or someone realizing the role no longer fits.',
    array[
