    'sexual-cognition-arousal-attention-map',
    'Sexual response taxonomy',
    'Connects fantasy, attention, anxiety, cognitive interpretation, explicitness, and romantic context to arousal.',
    'Arousal is not only stimulus; it is attention plus interpretation. Track what captures focus, what interrupts it, what fantasy supplies, what anxiety blocks, what language feels too blunt or too vague, and whether the character reads the same cue as erotic, romantic, unsafe, embarrassing, or irrelevant. Visual cues, romantic atmosphere, smell, sound, touch, memory, and text can all work differently depending on history. In prose, show the shift through attention: what the character notices, avoids, replays, or cannot stop thinking about.',
