  (
    'core-orgasm-desire-feedback-map',
    'Orgasm and Desire Feedback Map',
    'orgasm-desire-feedback-map',
    'Sexual response taxonomy',
    'Routes orgasm reliability, pleasure learning, masturbation history, and sexual confidence into desire and avoidance patterns.',
    'Pleasure history feeds desire. If sex reliably ends in pressure, frustration, pain, invisibility, or no orgasm, desire may narrow or go quiet. If solo sex teaches the body faster than partnered sex does, that is information, not failure. Track orgasm reliability, multiple-orgasm capacity, pressure to perform, masturbation comfort, partner attention, pacing, touch specificity, and the emotional meaning attached to climax. Do not write orgasm as proof of consent, love, success, or gender truth; write it as one body event inside a larger relationship context.',
