-- - Publication metadata: Journal of Sex Research, Vol. 22, No. 2, pp. 184-205, May 1986.
-- - Authors: J. Kenneth Davidson, Sr., and Linda E. Hoffman.
-- - 22 pages, roughly 8k extracted words.
-- - The article studies fantasy frequency, sex-life satisfaction, fantasy content, arousal support,
--   partner comparison, guilt, disclosure, and older clinical assumptions that treated fantasy as pathology.
-- - These seeds modernize the vocabulary, preserve research caveats, and route coercive fantasy categories
--   as boundary/context material only. They do not treat fantasy content as real-world intent or endorsement.

