    'Routes fantasy as one possible tool for attention, arousal, orgasm, and pleasure pacing.',
    'When fantasy appears during partnered or solo sex, tag its function before judging its content. It may help a character focus, cross an arousal threshold, reduce pressure, intensify sensation, revisit a desired memory, reach orgasm, or protect a private inner room. Pair it with body response, rhythm, breath, attention, and after-feeling. If fantasy creates distance, guilt, comparison, or secrecy, route that into relationship consequence rather than treating the fantasy itself as automatically harmful.',
