      'rebound-function-map'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-breakup-self-concept-repair-map',
    'Breakup Self-Concept Repair Map',
    'breakup-self-concept-repair-map',
    'Relationship psychology taxonomy',
    'Routes post-breakup confidence, desirability, identity clarity, grief, and social disruption into scene pressure.',
    'After a breakup, track what changed besides relationship status: daily routine, social network, self-image, desirability, housing, money, future plan, friend group, sexuality, and trust. A new relationship may repair confidence or blur grief; being single may create freedom or loneliness. In prose, the useful pressure is specific: a deleted contact, an empty side of the bed, a new compliment landing too hard, or the first time someone asks what they want now.',
    array[
      'breakup-dissolution-context',
