    'Separates competence/status attraction cues from gender destiny, provider myths, and one-way power scripts.',
    'Use status-coded attraction material as character belief, not universal law. Usable cues: competence, steadiness, employment stability, follow-through, discipline, generosity, manners, clean self-presentation, and calm under small problems. Bias route: uniforms as automatic virtue, wealth as automatic worth, men as protectors by default, women as security-seeking by default, insecurity as disqualification, and poverty or unemployment as moral failure. For fiction, the belief can reveal class pressure, fear, fantasy, status hunger, or family history.',
