    'Boundary taxonomy',
    'Separates ordinary insecurity from possessiveness, public scenes, violence risk, and refusal to accept endings.',
    'Jealousy may be an emotion; possessive control is behavior. Track escalation markers: surveillance, accusations, public scenes, threats, blocking exits, anger at refusal, demands for exclusivity without reciprocity, revenge language, violence history, and inability to accept a breakup. Clean exits matter: no chasing, no bargaining after a clear no, no punishment, no smear campaign, no forced closure. In fiction, this can explain why a character acts guarded without endorsing control as romance.',
