    'Routes pose order, turn skipping, real-time play, forum play, freeform play, and tavern scenes.',
    'Classify the pacing mode before generating. Real-time mode favors shorter readable actions and quick response loops. Forum or email mode allows slower, richer paragraphs. Tavern or sandbox mode needs awareness of multiple characters and open entry points. Pose order protects readability: do not skip a waiting player without an agreed timeout, do not answer for another PC, and do not make a scene event impossible for someone to respond to. Every turn should leave the next player a clean handle.',
