    'Roleplay boundary taxonomy',
    'Detects godmodding, puppeting without permission, forced outcomes, retcon needs, and control-boundary breaches.',
    'Use this router when a roleplay turn controls someone else too much. Agency breaches include deciding another PC''s action, thought, consent, injury, death, reaction, success, failure, or emotional conclusion; seizing GM canon; ignoring established limits; or forcing a scene outcome. Repair routes: ask OOC, narrow the action to an attempt, give the other player the response, roll or arbitrate, retcon the impossible beat, or pause if the breach keeps repeating.',
