    'Compersion, Jealousy, and Autonomy Map',
    'compersion-jealousy-autonomy-map',
    'Relationship psychology taxonomy',
    'Separates compersion, jealousy, possessiveness, reassurance needs, autonomy, and comparison fear.',
    'Map compersion and jealousy as skills under pressure, not as moral grades. Compersion may be easy, aspirational, absent, fragile, performative, or mixed with grief. Jealousy may point to time scarcity, comparison, fear of replacement, broken agreement, secrecy, inequity, loneliness, status wound, or real neglect. Autonomy does not mean abandonment; reassurance does not mean control. Good scenes let two truths stand at once: a partner can want freedom and still need care.',
