    'Classify sexual motive without flattening the character. Common motive clusters include pleasure, curiosity, adventure, love, bonding, validation, revenge, jealousy, status, duty, partner-pleasing, relief, exchange, experimentation, and self-discovery. A motive can be mixed: a character may want pleasure and reassurance, or curiosity and revenge, or love and obligation. For fiction, the motive should change behavior, pacing, dialogue, risk tolerance, and aftermath.',
