    'Map the visible problem beside the private one. Outer track: goal, obstacle, stakes, antagonist countermove, loss, deadline, and changed tactic. Inner track: fear, wound, lie, desire, defense, avoided truth, and changed behavior. The two tracks should touch in scene action. If the outer plot can be solved without emotional change, the arc may be ornamental. If the inner change never affects choices, it may be therapy notes instead of story.',
    array[
