    'antagonist-countermove-chain-engine',
    'Plot pressure taxonomy',
    'Turns antagonist opposition into a readable escalation chain of move, countermove, adaptation, and cost.',
    'Build antagonist pressure as a chain. The protagonist acts, the antagonist answers, the answer changes the field, and the protagonist must adapt. Each countermove should reveal something: capability, motive, blind spot, cruelty, longing, status, fear, or strategic intelligence. Escalation works best when the antagonist blocks the immediate goal while tightening the inner wound. The scene should leave a sharper problem, not just a louder one.',
    array[
