    'Classify infidelity questions by what they are trying to reveal. Fact questions ask what happened, when, where, with whom, and what was shared. Meaning questions ask what the affair gave the involved partner, what they said to themselves, whether love or future plans were named, and what the affair partner represented. Risk questions ask about secrecy, safer-sex breaches, prior patterns, and current contact. Repair questions ask what accountability, boundaries, testing, disclosure, and changed behavior would make trust possible again.',
