    'Relationship repair taxonomy',
    'Classifies behaviors that destabilize repair after infidelity without treating one recovery model as universal law.',
    'Use this map for the aftermath of an affair, hidden sexual behavior, or severe romantic betrayal. Recovery-failure buckets: pretending the affair is over before contact is ended, trickle-truth disclosure, defensiveness, treating hurt words as final truth, living as if nothing changed, defending the affair partner, avoiding the betrayed partner''s feelings, pointing to the betrayed partner''s flaws too soon, triggering reminders carelessly, lying again, refusing recovery support, inconsistency, broken agreements, demanding forgiveness, withholding answers, silent punishment, recruiting allies, formula thinking, threats, and using children as leverage. Store the behavior, motive, harm, and repair consequence separately.',
