      'infidelity-disclosure-question',
      'affair-permission-story',
      'psych-conflict-repair',
      'belief-source-reference'
    ],
    array['JanitorAI', 'SillyTavern', 'MarinaraTavern']
  ),
  (
    'core-trickle-truth-disclosure-map',
    'Trickle Truth Disclosure Map',
    'trickle-truth-disclosure-map',
    'Relationship repair taxonomy',
    'Tracks partial truth, delayed revelation, spun truth, withheld details, and repeated trust collapse after betrayal.',
    'Trickle truth is not only missing information; it is repeated injury. Track what was disclosed, what was withheld, what was minimized, what was discovered later, and what each new reveal does to trust. A character may leak facts from fear, shame, control, self-protection, denial, or strategy. The betrayed partner may need fact answers, meaning answers, health answers, timeline answers, or no more details. In modern prose, let disclosure live in the small tells: the pause before a date, a corrected word, a phone turned face down, the exhausted sentence that changes the whole room.',
    array[
