    'When a character seeks a group, separate need from ideology. Needs can include belonging, safety, confidence, mentorship, family substitute, professional access, social proof, escape from loneliness, protection from threat, or a sharper public identity. Pressure appears when the group asks for loyalty before trust is earned. Scene cues: defending the group too quickly, minimizing danger, craving an invitation, fearing expulsion, mistaking attention for care, or accepting small humiliations because exclusion would hurt more.',
