    'Campus status systems trade access for compliance. Track what the group grants: party invitations, introductions, romantic visibility, career network, housing, protection, borrowed confidence, or a ready-made public identity. Then track the bill: dues, time, secrecy, loyalty tests, conformity, alcohol pressure, tolerance of misogyny or exclusion, silence after harm, or fear of losing the group. Modern prose should hold both truths: a group can feel like home and still ask for too much.',
