    'Treat fantasy disclosure as a ladder. Start with low-risk curiosity, move through turn-ons, memory, compliments, and soft hypotheticals, then ask about explicit fantasies only when trust and reciprocity are present. Store what is invitation, what is confession, what is joke, what is test balloon, and what requires negotiation before enactment. In fiction, fantasy talk should reveal desire and fear at the same time: what the character wants, what they are afraid to ask for, and what they need to hear before they dare say more.',
