values
  (
    'core-rapport-ladder-taxonomy',
    'Rapport Ladder Taxonomy',
    'rapport-ladder-taxonomy',
    'Relationship taxonomy',
    'Adds social-capital levels for how characters move from strangers to one-on-one allies to introduced members of a wider circle.',
    'Classify rapport by social access. Level 1: no rapport. Level 2: one-on-one rapport, where two people can comfortably spend time alone. Level 3: introductory rapport, where one person will introduce the other into their social circle. Level 4: commodity rapport, where people seek the character out because the connection itself has social value. Level 5: rapport-defining, where the character becomes a benchmark, trendsetter, or defining node in the group. This is useful for friend groups, elite circles, workplace politics, found family, and social-climber arcs.',
    array[
