    'attraction-taxonomy-router',
    'Attraction and relationship taxonomy',
    'Routes attraction material into safe, character-driven cue systems instead of pickup-script advice.',
    'Classify attraction through observable cues, character context, and consent. Buckets: physical presentation, grooming, style, voice, scent, posture, gaze, smile, proximity, competence, status, confidence, social proof, humor, novelty, mystery, approach, responsiveness, reciprocal investment, dating logistics, text/phone pacing, jealousy, conflict, and space. Do not treat vulnerability, intoxication, youth, isolation, dependency, fear, or confusion as attraction fuel. Those belong in risk routing, not seduction logic. For fiction, attraction should reveal desire, insecurity, projection, class/status pressure, personal taste, and changed behavior under emotional stakes.',
    array[
