    'Attraction and relationship taxonomy',
    'Separates mutual interest cues from exploitability, impairment, pressure, and misread-signal risk.',
    'When reading attraction cues, separate three layers. Interest cues: sustained reciprocal attention, active approach, playful mirroring, voluntary proximity, initiated touch, clear verbal invitation, enthusiastic follow-through, and relaxed re-engagement. Ambiguous cues: politeness, nervous laughter, revealing clothing, social friendliness, alcohol-present environments, silence, delayed replies, shyness, jealousy, and public performance. Risk cues: impairment, isolation, dependency, fear, fatigue, youth, coercion, pressure, deception, dissociation, refusal, or inability to leave. Only the first layer can support escalation. The second needs slower pacing and clarification. The third must halt erotic escalation and route to care, distance, or safety.',
