    'Separates sexual closeness, emotional closeness, communication skill, self-disclosure, and unmet needs.',
    'Classify intimacy on two axes: sexual intimacy and emotional intimacy. Sexual intimacy includes physical touch, arousal, orgasm, sexual preference, fantasy, and body confidence. Emotional intimacy includes self-disclosure, trust, private thought, grief, hope, care, fear, affection, reassurance, and being emotionally present. Gaps create story pressure: physically close but emotionally hidden, emotionally safe but sexually blocked, sexually compatible but values-mismatched, emotionally intense but physically avoidant, or mutually intimate but stressed by outside demands. Repair routes include listening, naming expectations, asking for needs, negotiating differences, and changing behavior.',
